  "Id": 1729,
  "Title": "Inauguration of the Aga Khan Garden, Alberta",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "University of Alberta and AKU have been working in partnership for decades.",
  "GlobalNews": true,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassB2D4486BB5624D44936A8AECD00EA1BA\"><div>Lieutenant Governor of Alberta Lois Mitchell, Alberta Premier Rachel Notley and His Highness the Aga Khan inaugurated the new Aga Khan Garden, Alberta, the northern-most Islamic garden in the world, and the first garden of its kind in western Canada.</div><div><br>The Chancellor\u2019s gift of spectacular Aga Khan Garden is a symbol of the continued intellectual, educational and cultural collaboration between the University of Alberta and the Aga Khan Development Network.</div><div><br>The University of Alberta and Aga Khan University have been working together for decades. In 2017, the universities <a href=\"/news/Pages/News_Details.aspx?nid=NEWS-001173\" target=\"_blank\">renewed a memorandum of understanding</a>, originally signed in 2006, to move forward their respective goals of increasing global engagement and promoting equitable human development for citizens around the world.</div><div><br>Learn more on <a href=\"https&#58;//www.akdn.org/press-release/aga-khan-garden-inaugurated-canada\" target=\"_blank\">AKDN</a> and <a href=\"https&#58;//www.ualberta.ca/news-and-events\" target=\"_blank\">UoA</a> websites.\u200b<br></div></div>",
